        "line_end": 1,
        "exact_text": "I am a math teacher, and I want to create an educational animation for my students to visualize why matrices can perform linear transformations on vectors. Please create an animation as linear_transform.mp4 with at least 5 seconds, showing: 1) A 2D coordinate system with labeled x/y axes; 2) The standard basis vectors $\\hat{\\imath} = (1,0)$ and $\\hat{\\jmath} = (0,1)$; 3) A 2x2 transformation matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$ and demonstrate how matrix columns represent where basis vectors land after transformation; 4) Show an arbitrary vector $\\vec{v} = (1,1)$ and demonstrate that $\\vec{v}$ transforms to $A\\vec{v}$ by following the transformed basis vectors ($\\vec{v} = 1 \\cdot \\hat{\\imath} + 1 \\cdot \\hat{\\jmath}$ becomes $\\vec{v}' = 1 \\cdot \\hat{\\imath}' + 1 \\cdot \\hat{\\jmath}'$); 5) Explain visually why this preserves linearity (addition and scalar multiplication). ",
        "source_sha256": "9afbd24ae8ab7398b4b3b94e0e7072e6dd89962b38c5174019827bbd4b28d96f",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    }
  ],
